# JS Runtime Native Dispatch ids (nogc_sync_mut tier).
# These lived in runtime.spl, but that module imports js/engine/interpreter.spl
# back (a JsRuntime embeds a JsInterpreter), and every interpreter module
# val-imports these ids. A val import from a still-loading module is rejected,
# so the ids live in this import-free module and runtime.spl re-exports them
# via `export use` -- `std.js.engine.runtime` stays the single import site.
# Ids intentionally diverge from the common tier's copies where noted
# historically (single source of truth is THIS file for these names).

